WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.629 --> 00:00:11.650
I was nine years old when I first started
playing organized hockey, and it was just

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:13.490
something that became a passion.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:18.130
It was a case where I was playing football
in high school, but our games were Saturday

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.130
afternoons.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:22.689
I would play football in the afternoon, and
then go play hockey at night.

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:26.480
Because my high school didn't have a hockey
team, I started the hockey team there my senior

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.609
year also.

00:00:27.609 --> 00:00:33.070
So when I came to Hillsdale, my first year,
all I wanted was to get good grades because,

00:00:33.070 --> 00:00:39.360
as I said, my dream was to transfer from Hillsdale
so I could find a school to play hockey.

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:43.650
Because I'd been Dean's list my freshman year,
I decided, well, I'm going to see if I can

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:44.880
get a group together.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.170
I put up posters around the campus, asking
for any students who might be interested in

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:50.280
forming a hockey club.

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:56.190
Out of the blue, we had I think 10 or 12 skaters,
some better than the others.

00:00:56.190 --> 00:01:02.840
That first ragtag team, we used to skate on
Baw Beese Lake or the arb pond.

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:07.720
When we could get some money together, we
would go up to the University of Michigan.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:11.340
Usually at midnight or 1:00 was the only time
that we could get the ice.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:15.450
We'd pile into three or four cars and drive
up there and then skate.

00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:20.399
That first year we had four games, and then
the last game of the season we drove down

00:01:20.399 --> 00:01:25.630
to Columbus, Ohio to play the Ohio State JV's
and we beat them 17 to nothing.

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:28.409
It was a great way to end our first season.

00:01:28.409 --> 00:01:34.670
I think the thing that really brought success
to the program, they built an arena in Jackson.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:42.159
In '68, '69, the last game of the season was
the Purdue game and it was standing room only.

00:01:42.159 --> 00:01:44.840
You couldn't find a place even to walk.

00:01:44.840 --> 00:01:49.299
Here's little Hillsdale College playing Purdue
University.

00:01:49.299 --> 00:01:54.409
We were losing two to nothing after the first
period and we beat Purdue 14 to two.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:58.829
When the students went back to campus there
was such a buzz about the hockey team that

00:01:58.829 --> 00:02:02.909
that's when they put together a petition and
they petitioned the Board of Trustees to make

00:02:02.909 --> 00:02:05.639
it a varsity sport and the board approved
it.

00:02:05.639 --> 00:02:12.730
I coached from 1962 to 1963 and when I came
back I coached from 1966 to 1974.

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:15.420
I never planned to coach.

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.800
I'd wanted to skate.

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:22.550
I wound up coaching and really through books
and other things had to teach myself.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:27.200
Jeff called and left a message on my phone,
he said, "I have to tell you, you know, you're

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.470
being inducted into the athletic hall of fame
at Hillsdale College."

00:02:30.470 --> 00:02:35.080
He told me that a lot of the younger players,
they'd sent a letter off to the director of

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.080
athletics.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:37.900
It was humbling.

00:02:37.900 --> 00:02:43.750
I was very shocked, very surprised, but obviously
to have it happen now was just totally amazing

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:46.020
and as I said, extremely humbling.

